          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Meshes are towers of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratified+space#constructible_strat_bun"} constructible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratified+space#stratified_bundle"} stratified bundles
            whose fibers are points or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framing"} framed
            stratified 1-manifolds. Meshes play a central role in the local description of directed (namely,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+space#framed_spaces"} framed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+complex"} cell
            and
            %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poincar%C3%A9_duality#Dual_cell_structures"} dual-cell
            complexes.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Meshes are certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratified+space"} stratified spaces
            with additional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            (namely, structure that records spatial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+space"} directions
            via a notion of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+space#framed_spaces"} framings
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framing"} ordinary sense
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em 1-mesh
              is a framed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \leq 1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratification"} stratification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              whose strata are open
              = succeed "-disks," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi l
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi l
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l \leq 1
          %p
            Contractability implies that any 1-mesh framed embeds in standard framed
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            = succeed "." do
              %em mesh-trivializations
          %p
            To prepare for the definition of a bundle of 1-meshes, recall, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratified+space#fundamental_categories"}
              fundamental
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "italic"}
                    %mi trat
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Cat
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E} : \mathcal{S}\mathit{trat} \to \mathbf{Cat}_\infty
            maps
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratified+space#conical_strat"} conical stratifications
            to their fundamental
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-categories"} ∞-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratified+space#exit_entrance_conv"} entrance paths
            (which is the opposite convention to working with
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratified+space#exit_entrance_conv"} exit paths
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              For simplicity, below one can replace the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              with the ordinary fundamental
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{E}
              = succeed "-meshes" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-mesh" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %em bundles
              will differ).
          %p
            The following definition abstractly characterizes bundles of 1-meshes (see Rmk.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#rmk_mesh_bundles_concrete"}
            for an elaboration). We assume all stratifications to be conical.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em 1-mesh bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : (M,f) \to (B,g)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratified+space#stratified_bundle"} stratified bundle
              with 1-mesh fibers
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (M_x, f_x)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \hookrightarrow (\pi_B : B \times \mathbb{R} \to B)
              into the trivial
              = succeed "-bundle" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}(p)
                is an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conduch%C3%A9+functor"} exponentiable fibration
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}(p_{(0)})
                is an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration#opfibrations_and_bifibrations"} opfibration
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}(p_{(1)})
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} fibration
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
